{
  "slug": "weegloo",
  "name": "Weegloo",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Weegloo is a headless CMS that lets you manage and interact with Content Types, Content, and Media in a simple, human-friendly way.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **15 skills** and **2 MCP servers**.\n\n- **Skills** (15): `weegloo-api-query-optimization` (Weegloo list APIs - projection with select (include/exclude, object paths), list-as-single via sys.id, batch fetch with sys.id[in], prefetch…), `weegloo-cda-publish` (CDA (and ACDA) expose only published resources with publish-time values; CMA create/update needs explicit publish; ACMA create/delete auto-publish/auto-unpublish…), `weegloo-cma-json-patch` (Weegloo CMA/ACMA updates - prefer HTTP PATCH with RFC 6902 JSON Patch over PUT for smaller payloads; PUT…), `weegloo-create-content-type` (Creates or designs a ContentType in Weegloo — content modeling, schema and field design, choosing a field's type), `weegloo-default-locale` (Use when creating or updating Content in any localized or multi-language scenario), `weegloo-delivery-access-token` (Create Weegloo DeliveryAccessToken (CDA) via CMA-bind role.sys.id to the intended least-privilege SpaceRole only; never Administrator or first list…), `weegloo-list-pagination` (Weegloo list APIs return links.self, links.next, links.prev for pagination; combine with first-page query params (e.g), `weegloo-marketapp-packaging` (Build-time rules for any WebHosting that will (or may) be packaged into a MarketApp AppBundle), and 7 more\n- **MCP servers** (2): `weegloo`, `weegloo-upload`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install weegloo@claude-community` from `weeglooapi/weegloo-mcp-plugin` (`plugins/weegloo`).",
